Negative control for the "open-to-read" verb (FE-3091 design §3).

Strips the `detail` branch from `pressRowAction`, so a declared `detail`
control no longer opens the read overlay — it falls through to the handoff
branch (no handoff) and then to a live action of the same name, which the read
verb never was. The read overlay never opens.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the detail-verb spec — pressing a `detail`-flagged row action must open
the read overlay (a DetailDialog), never call a live action.

